  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1139 PM CDT SAT AUG 15 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will continue to dominate the forecast into\nthe middle of next week, keeping heat index values well into Heat\nAdvisory criteria. Rain chances will also start to decrease by\ntoday, as the ridge shifts slightly to the west. This will allow\nfor more convergence aloft up north, keeping the isolated rain\nchances mainly in our southern counties. These storms will\ncontinue to be capable of producing heavy rainfall and gusty\nwinds given the incredibly unstable airmass.\n\nBy the middle of next week, the ridge will slide to the west even\nmore, allowing for the region to shift into northwest flow\nbetween the ridge to the west, and a trough over the Ohio Valley.\nGuidance is already in pretty good agreement with a surface\nboundary working into the region during this time, with medium\nconfidence in increased rain chances, and afternoon highs\ndropping a few degrees by Friday. While this won't be a wholesale\nswing, any relief will be welcomed given this extended pattern\nwe've been stuck in.\n\n/44/",
